angular-momentum-vector.conceptual_definition:
The formula 
$ \mathbf{L} = \mathbf{I} \cdot \boldsymbol{\omega} $
describes the relationship between the angular momentum vector (
$ \mathbf{L} $
) of a rigid body and its rotational motion. It states that the angular momentum is the product of the body's moment of inertia tensor (
$ \mathbf{I} $
) and its angular velocity vector (
$ \boldsymbol{\omega} $
). This equation is a vector equation, and the dot product here represents a tensor-vector multiplication.
